/-!
# The cotangent complex of a quotient by a Koszul-regular ideal

Let `A → B` be a surjective ring map whose kernel `I` is a Koszul-regular ideal — Tag 07CV (2),
`Ideal.IsKoszulRegular`. Then `L_{B/A}` is quasi-isomorphic to the conormal module `I/I²` placed
in cohomological degree `-1`, that is, to `I/I²[1]`; this is **[Stacks, Tag 08SK]**.

The proof is the source's. A Koszul-regular ideal is only *locally* generated by a Koszul-regular
sequence: `Ideal.IsKoszulRegular I` says that at every prime `p ⊇ I` there is a `g ∉ p` such that
`I` becomes generated by a Koszul-regular sequence in `A_g = Localization.Away g`. For each such
`g` the localized map `A_g → B_g` is again surjective, with kernel the localized ideal
(`IsLocalization.map_surjective_of_surjective` and `IsLocalization.ker_map`), so
**[Stacks, Tag 08SJ]** — `CommAlgCat.isZero_homology_cotangentComplex_of_isKoszulRegular_sequence`
— gives `H^i(L_{B_g/A_g}) = 0` for `i ≤ -2`.

Those `g` whose images generate the unit ideal of `B`: if they did not, a maximal ideal of `B`
containing all of them would pull back to a prime of `A` containing `I`, and Koszul-regularity
produces at that prime a `g` which is in the cover and outside the maximal ideal. So the
`B`-module `H^i(L_{B/A})` vanishes as soon as each of its localizations `H^i(L_{B/A}) ⊗_B B_g`
does, and [Stacks, Tag 08SF] — that `L_{B_g/A_g} = L_{B/A} ⊗^𝐋_B B_g` — identifies that
localization with `H^i(L_{B_g/A_g})`, because `B → B_g` is flat so degreewise extension of
scalars computes the derived one and commutes with homology. That is the one vanishing
`StacksFrontier.Cotangent.SurjectionSingleDegree` needs in order to identify `L_{B/A}` with
`I/I²[1]`.

## Main definitions

* `CommAlgCat.awayMap`: the map `A_g → B_g` induced by `A → B` on the principal localizations
  away from `g` and from its image.
* `CommAlgCat.KernelKoszulRegularAway`: the kernel of `A → B` becomes generated by a
  Koszul-regular sequence in `A_g`.
* `CommAlgCat.HasLocalizedCotangentComplexAt`: [Stacks, Tag 08SF] at the single localization
  `A_g → B_g` of the given surjection — the carried hypothesis.
* `CommAlgCat.HasFundamentalTriangleAtPolynomialRetractions`: the hypothesis that Tag 08SJ
  already carries, named so that it can be carried pointwise at the localizations.
* `CommAlgCat.koszulCover`: the set of images in `B` of the elements `g` of
  `CommAlgCat.KernelKoszulRegularAway`.

## Main results

* `CommAlgCat.span_koszulCover_eq_top`: the cover generates the unit ideal of `B`.
* `CommAlgCat.isZero_extendScalars_homology_cotangentComplex_away`: for `g` as above,
  `H^i(L_{B/A}) ⊗_B B_g = 0` for `i ≤ -2`.
* `CommAlgCat.isZero_homology_cotangentComplex_of_isKoszulRegular`: `H^i(L_{B/A}) = 0` for
  `i ≤ -2`, when `ker(A → B)` is a Koszul-regular ideal.
* `CommAlgCat.nonempty_cotangentComplex_iso_single_of_isKoszulRegular`:
  **[Stacks, Tag 08SK]**.

## The carried hypotheses

Two hypotheses are carried, neither of them the conclusion.

**[Stacks, Tag 08SF]**, `cotangent-lemma-localize`, is not proved in this library and no
declaration carries that tag; the library has no localization statement for the cotangent complex
under any other name either. It is carried as `h08SF`, in the pointwise form
`CommAlgCat.HasLocalizedCotangentComplexAt A B g`, quantified only over the `g` at which the
Koszul-regularity of the kernel actually produces a generating sequence — so the hypothesis is as
weak as the proof allows, in the style of `CommAlgCat.HasFundamentalTriangleAt`. Its content is an
isomorphism in `D(B_g)`

`L_{B_g/A_g} ≅ L_{B/A} ⊗_B B_g`,

between two whole complexes. It speaks of no homology in any degree, of no single module, and of
the conormal module not at all; in particular it is not the conclusion restated, nor the vanishing
`H^i(L_{B/A}) = 0` which is what this file derives. It is a statement about a *different* ring
map, `A_g → B_g`, and all of the work of Tag 08SK is what it is combined with: the Koszul-regular
generating sequence in `A_g`, Tag 08SJ applied to it, the flatness of `B → B_g`, and the descent
from the cover.

**Proposition 08QX** is carried for the same reason, and in the same shape, as in
`StacksFrontier.Cotangent.KoszulRegularQuotient`: Tag 08SJ there carries it because Tag 08SI
(`CommAlgCat.nonempty_cotangentComplex_retraction_iso_single`) does, 08QX not being proved in
this library — see the `No @[stacks 08QX]` section of
`StacksFrontier/Cotangent/Triangle/Distinguished.lean`. Since Tag 08SJ is applied here to the
localized maps `A_g → B_g`, the hypothesis is needed for the towers `A_g → P → A_g` with `P` a
polynomial algebra over `A_g` carrying a retraction, and is carried in exactly that form,
pointwise in `g` as well.

## Implementation notes

**The algebra structure on `B_g` over `A_g`.** `Localization.Away g` acts on
`Localization.Away (algebraMap A B g)` through `IsLocalization.map`, which is not an instance in
Mathlib; `CommAlgCat.awayAlgebra` names that structure and it is made a local instance, so that
`CommAlgCat.of (Localization.Away g) (Localization.Away (algebraMap A B g))` can be written
without a `letI` in every statement. There is no competing instance for it.

**The descent.** `CommAlgCat.isZero_of_isZero_extendScalars_away` is the Zariski-local vanishing
of a module in the form in which it is needed here, with the localizations presented as
`ModuleCat.extendScalars` rather than as `LocalizedModule`; the bridge between the carrier
`B_g ⊗_B M` of the former — whose `B`-module structure on `B_g` is `Module.compHom` along the
ring map — and the plain tensor product is
`StacksDraft.TorAmplitude.FaithfullyFlat.extendScalarsCarrierEquiv`. The same statement appears,
privately and for a different purpose, as `isZero_of_isZero_localizations` of
`StacksFrontier/Homology/TorAmplitude/Local.lean`.

**One universe.** The rings all lie in a single universe, as they must: Tag 08SJ is stated for
`R : Type u` and `S : CommAlgCat.{u} R`, and `B_g` is a localization of `B`, so `B` has to live
in the universe of `A`.

## References

* [Stacks Project, Tag 08SK](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/08SK)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 08SJ](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/08SJ)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 08SF](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/08SF)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 08SI](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/08SI)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 08QX](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/08QX)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 07CV](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/07CV)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 00EO](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/00EO)
-/

@[expose] public noncomputable section

open CategoryTheory CategoryTheory.Limits

universe u

namespace CommAlgCat

attribute [local instance] HasDerivedCategory.standard

section Away

variable (A : Type u) [CommRing A] (B : CommAlgCat.{u} A)

/-- The powers of `g` map into the powers of its image, so the principal localization of `A`
away from `g` maps to the principal localization of `B` away from the image of `g`. -/
theorem powers_le_comap_powers (g : A) :
    Submonoid.powers g ≤
      (Submonoid.powers (algebraMap A (B : Type u) g)).comap (algebraMap A (B : Type u)) := by
  intro x hx
  obtain ⟨n, rfl⟩ := hx
  exact Submonoid.mem_comap.2
    (Submonoid.mem_powers_iff _ _ |>.2 ⟨n, (map_pow (algebraMap A (B : Type u)) g n).symm⟩)

/-- The map `A_g → B_g` induced by `A → B` on the principal localizations away from `g` and
away from the image of `g`. -/
def awayMap (g : A) :
    Localization.Away g →+* Localization.Away (algebraMap A (B : Type u) g) :=
  IsLocalization.map _ (algebraMap A (B : Type u)) (powers_le_comap_powers A B g)

/-- `B_g` as an `A_g`-algebra, through `CommAlgCat.awayMap`. This is a local instance of this
module; Mathlib has no instance for it. -/
@[instance_reducible]
def awayAlgebra (g : A) :
    Algebra (Localization.Away g) (Localization.Away (algebraMap A (B : Type u) g)) :=
  (awayMap A B g).toAlgebra

attribute [local instance] awayAlgebra

@[simp]
theorem algebraMap_awayAlgebra (g : A) :
    algebraMap (Localization.Away g) (Localization.Away (algebraMap A (B : Type u) g)) =
      awayMap A B g :=
  rfl

/-- `A_g → B_g` is again surjective. -/
theorem surjective_awayMap (h : Function.Surjective (algebraMap A (B : Type u))) (g : A) :
    Function.Surjective (awayMap A B g) := by
  have hloc : IsLocalization ((Submonoid.powers g).map (algebraMap A (B : Type u)))
      (Localization.Away (algebraMap A (B : Type u) g)) := by
    rw [Submonoid.map_powers]
    infer_instance
  exact IsLocalization.map_surjective_of_surjective (Submonoid.powers g) (Localization.Away g)
    (Localization.Away (algebraMap A (B : Type u) g)) h

/-- The kernel of `A_g → B_g` is the ideal generated by the image of the kernel of `A → B`. -/
theorem ker_awayMap (g : A) :
    RingHom.ker (awayMap A B g) =
      Ideal.map (algebraMap A (Localization.Away g)) (RingHom.ker (algebraMap A (B : Type u))) :=
  IsLocalization.ker_map (Localization.Away (algebraMap A (B : Type u) g))
    (algebraMap A (B : Type u)) (Submonoid.map_powers (algebraMap A (B : Type u)) g)

/-- The kernel of `A → B` becomes generated by a Koszul-regular sequence after localizing `A`
away from `g`. This is the condition that `Ideal.IsKoszulRegular`, Tag 07CV (2), supplies at
every prime containing the kernel. -/
def KernelKoszulRegularAway (g : A) : Prop :=
  ∃ (r : ℕ) (f : Fin r → Localization.Away g), Koszul.IsKoszulRegular f ∧
    Ideal.map (algebraMap A (Localization.Away g)) (RingHom.ker (algebraMap A (B : Type u))) =
      Ideal.span (Set.range f)

/-- **[Stacks, Tag 08SF] at the single localization `A_g → B_g` of `A → B`.** The cotangent
complex of the localized map is the degreewise extension of scalars of `L_{B/A}` along
`B → B_g` — which computes the derived one, `B → B_g` being flat. In the notation of the source,

`L_{B_g/A_g} = L_{B/A} ⊗^𝐋_B B_g`

in `D(B_g)`. The isomorphism is asked for existentially, no canonical arrow being available to
pin, as the source's equality is read elsewhere in this library.

This is the hypothesis carried by
`CommAlgCat.nonempty_cotangentComplex_iso_single_of_isKoszulRegular`; it is a statement about
the ring map `A_g → B_g` and about whole complexes, and mentions no
homology, no single module and no conormal module. It is the pointwise form, at one `g`, in the
style of `CommAlgCat.HasFundamentalTriangleAt`. -/
def HasLocalizedCotangentComplexAt (g : A) : Prop :=
  Nonempty (DerivedCategory.Q.obj (cotangentComplex (Localization.Away g)
      (CommAlgCat.of (Localization.Away g)
        (Localization.Away (algebraMap A (B : Type u) g)))) ≅
    DerivedCategory.Q.obj ((CochainComplex.extendScalarsLarge.{0, u, u}
      (algebraMap (B : Type u) (Localization.Away (algebraMap A (B : Type u) g)))).obj
      (cotangentComplex A B)))

end Away

/-- **Proposition 08QX for the towers `R → P → R` with `P` a polynomial algebra over `R`
carrying a retraction.** This is verbatim the hypothesis that
`CommAlgCat.nonempty_cotangentComplex_iso_single_of_isKoszulRegular_sequence`, Tag 08SJ, carries;
it is named here so that it can be carried pointwise at the localizations `A_g` to which Tag 08SJ
is applied. See the module docstring of `StacksFrontier.Cotangent.KoszulRegularQuotient`. -/
def HasFundamentalTriangleAtPolynomialRetractions (R : Type u) [CommRing R] : Prop :=
  ∀ (P : Type u) [CommRing P] [Algebra R P] [Algebra P R] [IsScalarTower R P R],
    Algebra.IsPolynomialAlgebra R P → HasFundamentalTriangleAt R P R

section Descent

/-- A module that vanishes after extension of scalars to the localization away from every member
of a set generating the unit ideal vanishes. This is [Stacks, Tag 00EO] (1) in the shape needed
below, with the localizations presented as `ModuleCat.extendScalars`. -/
theorem isZero_of_isZero_extendScalars_away (R : Type u) [CommRing R] (s : Set R)
    (hs : Ideal.span s = ⊤) (N : ModuleCat.{u} R)
    (hN : ∀ t : s, IsZero ((ModuleCat.extendScalars
      (algebraMap R (Localization.Away (t : R)))).obj N)) :
    IsZero N := by
  rw [ModuleCat.isZero_iff_subsingleton]
  refine subsingleton_of_forall_eq 0 fun x => ?_
  refine Module.eq_zero_of_isLocalized_span s hs
    (fun t => TensorProduct R (Localization.Away (t : R)) (N : Type u))
    (fun t => TensorProduct.mk R (Localization.Away (t : R)) (N : Type u) 1) x ?_
  intro t
  have hsub : Subsingleton
      ((ModuleCat.extendScalars (algebraMap R (Localization.Away (t : R)))).obj N : Type u) :=
    ModuleCat.isZero_iff_subsingleton.mp (hN t)
  have hsub' : Subsingleton (TensorProduct R (Localization.Away (t : R)) (N : Type u) ) :=
    (StacksDraft.TorAmplitude.FaithfullyFlat.extendScalarsCarrierEquiv R
      (Localization.Away (t : R)) N).toEquiv.subsingleton_congr.mp hsub
  exact Subsingleton.elim _ _

end Descent

section KoszulRegularIdeal

variable (A : Type u) [CommRing A] (B : CommAlgCat.{u} A)

attribute [local instance] awayAlgebra

/-- The images in `B` of the elements `g` of `A` at which the kernel of `A → B` becomes generated
by a Koszul-regular sequence. -/
def koszulCover : Set (B : Type u) :=
  {b | ∃ g : A, b = algebraMap A (B : Type u) g ∧ KernelKoszulRegularAway A B g}

/-- **The cover generates the unit ideal.** Were it not so, a maximal ideal of `B` containing it
would pull back to a prime of `A` containing the kernel, and the Koszul-regularity of the kernel
produces at that prime a `g` lying in the cover and outside the maximal ideal. -/
theorem span_koszulCover_eq_top
    (hI : Ideal.IsKoszulRegular (RingHom.ker (algebraMap A (B : Type u)))) :
    Ideal.span (koszulCover A B) = ⊤ := by
  by_contra hne
  obtain ⟨m, hm, hle⟩ := Ideal.exists_le_maximal (Ideal.span (koszulCover A B)) hne
  have hmax : m.IsMaximal := hm
  have hker : RingHom.ker (algebraMap A (B : Type u)) ≤
      Ideal.comap (algebraMap A (B : Type u)) m := by
    intro a ha
    change algebraMap A (B : Type u) a ∈ m
    rw [RingHom.mem_ker.mp ha]
    exact m.zero_mem
  obtain ⟨g, hg, r, f, hf, hspan⟩ :=
    hI ⟨Ideal.comap (algebraMap A (B : Type u)) m, Ideal.comap_isPrime _ _⟩ hker
  exact hg (hle (Ideal.subset_span ⟨g, rfl, r, f, hf, hspan⟩))

/-- **The vanishing of [Stacks, Tag 08SK], at one localization.** For `g` at which the kernel of
the surjection `A → B` becomes generated by a Koszul-regular sequence, the localization
`H^i(L_{B/A}) ⊗_B B_g` vanishes in the degrees `i ≤ -2`.

Tag 08SJ applies to the localized surjection `A_g → B_g`, giving `H^i(L_{B_g/A_g}) = 0`; the
carried Tag 08SF transports that to the degreewise extension of scalars of `L_{B/A}` along
`B → B_g`, and `B → B_g` being flat, extension of scalars commutes with homology. -/
theorem isZero_extendScalars_homology_cotangentComplex_away
    (h : Function.Surjective (algebraMap A (B : Type u))) (g : A)
    (hg : KernelKoszulRegularAway A B g)
    (h08SF : HasLocalizedCotangentComplexAt A B g)
    (h08QX : HasFundamentalTriangleAtPolynomialRetractions (Localization.Away g))
    (i : ℤ) (hi : i ≤ -2) :
    IsZero ((ModuleCat.extendScalars
      (algebraMap (B : Type u) (Localization.Away (algebraMap A (B : Type u) g)))).obj
      ((cotangentComplex A B).homology i)) := by
  obtain ⟨r, f, hf, hspan⟩ := hg
  obtain ⟨e⟩ := h08SF
  -- the localized surjection has kernel generated by the Koszul-regular sequence `f`
  have hker : RingHom.ker (awayMap A B g) = Ideal.span (Set.range f) := by
    rw [ker_awayMap A B g]
    exact hspan
  -- Tag 08SJ at `A_g → B_g`
  have hzloc : IsZero ((cotangentComplex (Localization.Away g)
      (CommAlgCat.of (Localization.Away g)
        (Localization.Away (algebraMap A (B : Type u) g)))).homology i) :=
    isZero_homology_cotangentComplex_of_isKoszulRegular_sequence (Localization.Away g)
      (CommAlgCat.of (Localization.Away g)
        (Localization.Away (algebraMap A (B : Type u) g)))
      (surjective_awayMap A B h g) f hf hker h08QX i hi
  -- pass to the derived category and across the carried Tag 08SF
  have hH : ∀ K : CochainComplex
      (ModuleCat.{u} (Localization.Away (algebraMap A (B : Type u) g))) ℤ,
      IsZero ((DerivedCategory.homologyFunctor _ i).obj (DerivedCategory.Q.obj K)) ↔
        IsZero (K.homology i) :=
    fun K => ((DerivedCategory.homologyFunctorFactors _ i).app K).isZero_iff
  have hmapped := (hH _).mp
    (((DerivedCategory.homologyFunctor _ i).mapIso e).isZero_iff.mp ((hH _).mpr hzloc))
  -- `B → B_g` is flat, so extension of scalars commutes with homology
  have hflat : (algebraMap (B : Type u)
      (Localization.Away (algebraMap A (B : Type u) g))).Flat :=
    RingHom.flat_algebraMap_iff.mpr inferInstance
  have hlim := StacksDraft.TorAmplitude.preservesFiniteLimits_extendScalars
    (f := algebraMap (B : Type u) (Localization.Away (algebraMap A (B : Type u) g))) hflat
  have hadd := StacksDraft.TorAmplitude.additive_extendScalars (f := algebraMap (B : Type u)
    (Localization.Away (algebraMap A (B : Type u) g))) hflat
  exact hmapped.of_iso (ShortComplex.mapHomologyIso ((cotangentComplex A B).sc i)
    (ModuleCat.extendScalars.{u, u, u} (algebraMap (B : Type u)
      (Localization.Away (algebraMap A (B : Type u) g))))).symm

/-- **`H^i(L_{B/A}) = 0` for `i ≤ -2`**, when `A → B` is surjective with Koszul-regular kernel.
This is the one vanishing that
`CommAlgCat.nonempty_cotangentComplex_iso_single_of_isZero_homology_le_negTwo` needs, and the
whole content of [Stacks, Tag 08SK]. -/
theorem isZero_homology_cotangentComplex_of_isKoszulRegular
    (h : Function.Surjective (algebraMap A (B : Type u)))
    (hI : Ideal.IsKoszulRegular (RingHom.ker (algebraMap A (B : Type u))))
    (h08SF : ∀ g : A, KernelKoszulRegularAway A B g → HasLocalizedCotangentComplexAt A B g)
    (h08QX : ∀ g : A, KernelKoszulRegularAway A B g →
      HasFundamentalTriangleAtPolynomialRetractions (Localization.Away g))
    (i : ℤ) (hi : i ≤ -2) :
    IsZero ((cotangentComplex A B).homology i) := by
  refine isZero_of_isZero_extendScalars_away (B : Type u) (koszulCover A B)
    (span_koszulCover_eq_top A B hI) _ ?_
  rintro ⟨b, g, rfl, hg⟩
  exact isZero_extendScalars_homology_cotangentComplex_away A B h g hg (h08SF g hg)
    (h08QX g hg) i hi

/-- **Stacks Project, Tag 08SK.** Let `A → B` be a surjective map of commutative rings whose
kernel `I` is a Koszul-regular ideal, Tag 07CV (2). Then `L_{B/A}` is quasi-isomorphic to
`I/I²[1]`, that is, isomorphic in `D(B)` to the conormal module `I/I²` placed in cohomological
degree `-1`.

The source's proof: locally on `Spec(A)` the ideal `I` is generated by a Koszul-regular sequence,
so [Stacks, Tag 08SJ] gives the vanishing of `H^i(L_{B_g/A_g})` for `i ≤ -2` over a cover, and
[Stacks, Tag 08SF] turns that into the vanishing of the localizations of `H^i(L_{B/A})`, hence of
`H^i(L_{B/A})` itself; then
`CommAlgCat.nonempty_cotangentComplex_iso_single_of_isZero_homology_le_negTwo` concludes.

See the module docstring for the two carried hypotheses. -/
@[stacks 08SK "the lemma for a Koszul-regular IDEAL (Tag 07CV (2), `Ideal.IsKoszulRegular`), \
  generalizing the sequence case Tag 08SJ \
  (`CommAlgCat.nonempty_cotangentComplex_iso_single_of_isKoszulRegular_sequence`). I/I^2 is the \
  conormal module of the surjection, as the cotangent module of the corresponding algebra \
  extension. TWO carried hypotheses, neither of them the conclusion. (1) h08SF: the localization \
  lemma of Tag 08SF, `cotangent-lemma-localize`, which is not proved in this library and which \
  no declaration here carries — it says L_{B_g/A_g} is isomorphic in D(B_g) to the degreewise \
  extension of scalars of L_{B/A} along the flat map B -> B_g, an isomorphism of whole complexes \
  for a DIFFERENT ring map A_g -> B_g, mentioning no homology in any degree, no single module \
  and no conormal module; it is carried pointwise, only at the g at which the Koszul-regularity \
  of the kernel produces a generating sequence. (2) h08QX: Proposition 08QX for the towers \
  A_g -> P -> A_g with P a polynomial algebra over A_g carrying a retraction — verbatim the \
  hypothesis that Tag 08SJ carries, inherited because Tag 08SJ is applied to the localized maps, \
  08QX not being proved in this library because the triangle the library has, Tag 08SD, needs \
  the middle map injective whereas an augmentation is surjective. Everything else is proved \
  outright: the Koszul cover generates the unit ideal, the localized map is surjective with \
  kernel the localized ideal, Tag 08SJ at it, the flatness of B -> B_g, and the Zariski descent \
  of the vanishing"]
theorem nonempty_cotangentComplex_iso_single_of_isKoszulRegular
    (h : Function.Surjective (algebraMap A (B : Type u)))
    (hI : Ideal.IsKoszulRegular (RingHom.ker (algebraMap A (B : Type u))))
    (h08SF : ∀ g : A, KernelKoszulRegularAway A B g → HasLocalizedCotangentComplexAt A B g)
    (h08QX : ∀ g : A, KernelKoszulRegularAway A B g →
      HasFundamentalTriangleAtPolynomialRetractions (Localization.Away g)) :
    Nonempty (DerivedCategory.Q.obj (cotangentComplex A B) ≅
      (DerivedCategory.singleFunctor (ModuleCat.{u} (B : Type u)) (-1)).obj
        (ModuleCat.of (B : Type u) (surjectionExtension A B h).Cotangent)) :=
  nonempty_cotangentComplex_iso_single_of_isZero_homology_le_negTwo A B h
    (isZero_homology_cotangentComplex_of_isKoszulRegular A B h hI h08SF h08QX)

end KoszulRegularIdeal

end CommAlgCat

end
